<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?><ns2:section xmlns:ns2="http://rest.cis.illinois.edu" id="49022" href="schedule/2013/fall/ARTH/540/49022.xml"><parents><calendarYear id="2013" href="schedule/2013.xml">2013</calendarYear><term id="120138" href="schedule/2013/fall.xml">Fall 2013</term><subject id="ARTH" href="schedule/2013/fall/ARTH.xml">Art--History</subject><course id="540" href="schedule/2013/fall/ARTH/540.xml">Seminar in Art 1750 to 1900</course></parents><sectionNumber>DO </sectionNumber><sectionTitle>Theories of Modernism</sectionTitle><statusCode>A</statusCode><sectionText>Topic: Theories of Modernism. This seminar examines some of the principal theories of modernism in painting.  Special emphasis will be placed on the rise of modernism in the second half of the nineteenth century, but twentieth-century modernism will also be part of our subject.  Scholars and writers whose work will be examined include Charles Baudelaire, Clement Greenberg, Michael Fried, and T.J. Clark.</sectionText><partOfTerm>1</partOfTerm><sectionStatusCode>A</sectionStatusCode><enrollmentStatus>UNKNOWN</enrollmentStatus><startDate>2013-08-26Z</startDate><endDate>2013-12-11Z</endDate><meetings><meeting id="0"><type code="CNF">Conference</type><start>07:00 PM</start><end>09:50 PM</end><daysOfTheWeek>R      </daysOfTheWeek><roomNumber>319</roomNumber><buildingName>Art and Design Building</buildingName><instructors><instructor lastName="O'Brien" firstName="D">O'Brien, D</instructor></instructors></meeting></meetings></ns2:section>